· Minimum carbothermic reactor energy: 3.37 MWh/tonne of liquid iron alloy.
· Total system energy (incl. MOXIE + agglomeration): 15.51 MWh/tonne (i.e., 15.51 kWh/kg).
· Reaction: $\text{Fe}_2\text{O}_3 + 3\text{C} \rightarrow 2\text{Fe} + 3\text{CO}$, $\Delta H^\circ = 492\,\text{kJ·mol}^{-1}$ (standard reference).
· Reduction temperature: ≈1060 °C under Martian atmospheric pressure.

D.8 CO₂‑Laser SLM of 316L

· Process: Selective Laser Melting with CO₂ laser on 316L stainless steel powder.
· Strength: Greater than fibre‑laser SLM under certain build‑up strategies.
· Hardness: Excellent; superior to fibre‑laser SLM in some configurations.
· Fracture strain: Reduced due to porosity and lack‑of‑melting defects.
· Conclusion: Feasible for non‑safety‑critical structural parts; requires post‑process heat treatment and fatigue characterisation before use in critical components.

